From 057106808eb97e75fde2b9a6d17048df276b8fde Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ritvik <ritvik2014@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 20:41:47 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 37/40] auto-fit: Mod+F doesn't reflow, a new window ends it;
 half-and-half action

Full width (maximize-column), maximized and fullscreen columns now count at
their normal width when columns are fitted, so making one full leaves the
others alone and the layout is whole again when it comes back. A new
column joining a workspace ends full width on the others (not fullscreen),
so it shares the screen instead of opening full beside them.

half-and-half: the focused column and its right neighbour (left at the end
of the strip) at half the screen each, both in view. With auto-fit they
keep half as their preference; without it they are sized by hand.
